WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.722
Run Prompt three after approving the
numbers.

2
00:00:02.722 --> 00:00:06.478
Ask Sites for the focused executive
dashboard website.

3
00:00:06.478 --> 00:00:10.710
Give it the metric contract and the
reconciled source context from the

4
00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.416
same chat.

5
00:00:11.416 --> 00:00:13.796
Start on June, All origins.

6
00:00:13.796 --> 00:00:20.288
The prompt specifies six cards, filters,
trends, source details and a spending

7
00:00:20.288 --> 00:00:20.829
illustration.

8
00:00:20.829 --> 00:00:26.216
It also specifies the reporting month, the
finalization date and the synthetic-data

9
00:00:26.216 --> 00:00:26.664
label.

10
00:00:26.664 --> 00:00:30.022
Let the first build finish before changing
the design.

11
00:00:30.022 --> 00:00:34.816
Use the reserved generation time rather
than turning the lesson into an

12
00:00:34.816 --> 00:00:36.015
open-ended layout exercise.

13
00:00:36.015 --> 00:00:40.799
The dashboard should provide a clear
overview, with the underlying evidence one

14
00:00:40.799 --> 00:00:41.596
action away.

15
00:00:41.596 --> 00:00:43.503
Open a metric definition.

16
00:00:43.503 --> 00:00:48.156
You should be able to identify its source
filename and field, its

17
00:00:48.156 --> 00:00:52.422
numerator and denominator where relevant,
its owner and its reporting date.

18
00:00:52.422 --> 00:00:55.829
Revenue should show the addition of the
two origin amounts.

19
00:00:55.829 --> 00:01:00.353
Transaction success should show the
combined completed and attempted counts.

20
00:01:00.353 --> 00:01:04.640
A viewer needs enough information to
understand the number even without

21
00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.200
downloading an Office file.

22
00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:10.690
Good typography helps reading; it cannot
replace those source checks.

23
00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:12.816
Select another reporting month.

24
00:01:12.816 --> 00:01:15.657
The cards and detail rows should use that
month.

25
00:01:15.657 --> 00:01:20.228
The trend charts retain the six-month
history for the selected customer origin

26
00:01:20.228 --> 00:01:22.132
and highlight your chosen month.

27
00:01:22.132 --> 00:01:26.749
This lets an executive compare the current
observation with its context.

28
00:01:26.749 --> 00:01:31.127
Read the scope note rather than assume
every chart has identical time

29
00:01:31.127 --> 00:01:31.491
coverage.

30
00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:32.908
Select January.

31
00:01:32.908 --> 00:01:38.154
Because December is absent from the source
pack, the prior-month comparison must

32
00:01:38.154 --> 00:01:39.028
say unavailable.

33
00:01:39.028 --> 00:01:43.352
Inventing a December baseline or showing a
zero change would conceal what

34
00:01:43.352 --> 00:01:45.154
the source does not contain.

35
00:01:45.154 --> 00:01:47.632
Now select June and Mobile-acquired.

36
00:01:47.632 --> 00:01:52.956
The reference checks are seventy ringgit
per verified customer, thirty-five percent

37
00:01:52.956 --> 00:01:55.860
activation and thirty percent contribution
margin.

38
00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:58.826
Revenue is four hundred and twenty
thousand ringgit.

39
00:01:58.826 --> 00:02:03.548
These are the business metrics attributed
to customers who originally joined through

40
00:02:03.548 --> 00:02:03.942
mobile.

41
00:02:03.942 --> 00:02:07.468
They are not a direct measurement of
traffic using the mobile app

42
00:02:07.468 --> 00:02:08.350
at this moment.

43
00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:13.272
Check that the cards, funnel, trends and
detail table all respect the

44
00:02:13.272 --> 00:02:14.092
chosen origin.

45
00:02:14.092 --> 00:02:18.302
Returning to All should restore six
hundred thousand ringgit of revenue.

46
00:02:18.302 --> 00:02:23.258
Filtering should change the underlying
inputs before the formula is evaluated.

47
00:02:23.258 --> 00:02:27.708
Do not keep a company-wide percentage
while displaying a cohort count.

48
00:02:27.708 --> 00:02:31.946
Do not add monthly unique people across
January to June and label

49
00:02:31.946 --> 00:02:34.771
the result unique customers for the whole
period.

50
00:02:34.771 --> 00:02:37.601
The same people may appear in several
months.

51
00:02:37.601 --> 00:02:39.866
Also inspect target verdicts.

52
00:02:39.866 --> 00:02:44.135
The supplied Board targets apply only to
June at company-wide scope.

53
00:02:44.135 --> 00:02:48.143
A mobile-only card can show its
measurement, but it should not inherit

54
00:02:48.143 --> 00:02:51.816
that company target as though a cohort
target had been approved.

55
00:02:51.816 --> 00:02:56.096
If a value or interaction fails, describe
the exact issue.

56
00:02:56.096 --> 00:03:01.162
State the expected result, ask ChatGPT to
trace the source inputs, formula

57
00:03:01.162 --> 00:03:06.228
and filter scope, and recheck June All and
June Mobile after the

58
00:03:06.228 --> 00:03:06.650
correction.

59
00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:09.246
Preserve the reviewed definitions and
layout.

60
00:03:09.246 --> 00:03:13.351
Avoid replacing the whole dashboard to
repair one calculation.

61
00:03:13.351 --> 00:03:17.503
Keep visual refinement to one specific
request during this hour.

62
00:03:17.503 --> 00:03:21.230
Save the reviewed version before
deployment or wider sharing.

63
00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:25.509
Pause now to run the prompt, operate the
controls and complete the

64
00:03:25.509 --> 00:03:26.578
three Mobile checks.

65
00:03:26.578 --> 00:03:31.493
If generation exceeds its allowance, use
the reference as an assisted recovery

66
00:03:31.493 --> 00:03:33.540
and record that assistance honestly.
